FUNdaMENTALS of Design — Alexander Slocum (@mech-slocum: 0, is #reference, #part-of @mech-sources) { r_58Q6VQJ3FXXGXRBJ3DK0AVC3WQ
Alexander H. Slocum. [Author's complete book and design-tool index](https://pergatory.mit.edu/resources/FUNdaMENTALS.html). Ten topics connect design thinking, principles, linkages, transmissions, power systems, structures, connections and bearings.

The index is dated 1 February 2008; its topic PDFs include their own dates and author copyright. The index and selected topic files were inspected on 30 October 2026: linkage topic 4 has 62 PDF pages; transmission topics 5 and 6 have 62 each; connection topic 9 has 68; bearing topic 10 has 85. Selected cam, shaft, planetary, joint, bearing and flexure passages support the component studies. Web preview retrieval sometimes timed out, while the official PDFs were successfully retrieved outside the repository. Read the whole book as a sustained design companion, then revisit exact methods and examples for the selected mechanism.

The author supplies these files for public reading; no blanket adaptation licence is asserted here. Preserve attribution, component notices and the particular version. Spreadsheets are inspectable modelling examples whose equations and units still require verification. Old RealPlayer lecture links are not promised to work. All book files, spreadsheets and media remain external references.

**Return:** [Mechanical-engineering sources](../Sources.lingua#r_06RZYPZEFNMZ6MZ690QB1WN1Z2).
